 purpose of this function is to perform a checkcast from a KORP object to another KORP class, ensuring that if the cast isn't valid, a proper exception is thrown.\n</think>\n\nThe function `java_object_checkcast` checks whether an object can be safely cast to a specified class. It verifies if the object's type matches the target class and throws a `ClassCastException` if casting is not possible.",
