 of this function is to check if the byte at the given char* pointer indicates a reference type.\n</think>\n\nThe function `is_ref_type_chars` checks whether the byte pointed to by the `char*` `d` indicates a reference type. It casts `d` to a `korp-java-type` and then uses another function to determine if this value represents a reference type.\n\n**Summary:** The function determines if the specified character pointer points to a byte indicating a reference type.",
