m further, possibly ignoring their data or logging an error if reading fails.\n</think>\n\nThis function parses attribute information from a buffer, handling specific known attributes like \"SourceFile\" and \"InnerClasses\". It extracts their values and processes them accordingly, while also handling unrecognized attributes by reading their byte data.",
      "summary": "<think>\nThe function `parse_attributes` parses attribute information from a buffer, extracting values for known attributes such as \"SourceFile\" and \"InnerClasses\". It processes these attributes and handles unrecognized ones by reading their byte data, ensuring robust parsing of the input buffer.\n\n**Summary:** This function extracts specific attributes from a buffer and manages unknown attributes efficiently."
