perclass method correctly. It iterates over each instance method in the superclass, checks for signature match, package compatibility, and whether the superclass's method is not default if they're from different packages. If all these are satisfied, it marks the current method as overriding.\n</think>\n\nThe function `override_superclass_method` checks if a class method overrides a superclass method correctly by verifying their signatures, ensuring the packages match (or handling defaults), and marking the method as overridden if conditions are met.\n\n**Summary:**  \nThis function determines whether a method in a subclass correctly overrides a method from its superclass by checking their signatures, package compatibility, and whether the superclass method is default. It returns true if all conditions are satisfied.",
      "summary": "<think>\nThe function `override_superclass_method` checks if a subclass method correctly overrides its superclass method by ensuring signature match, package compatibility, and non-default status of the superclass method, returning true upon successful override.\n\n**Summary:**  \nThis function verifies that a class's method properly overrides a superclass method, considering signature matching and package context. It ensures methods can be overridden as intended."
