 which are stored in a way that can be efficiently accessed by instances. It also handles the case where methods might override those from superclasses, ensuring proper handling of such overrides.\n</think>\n\nThe function prepares method information for a given class, setting up offsets for instance methods in a vtable structure. It handles both static and non-static methods, including those inherited from superclasses, ensuring efficient access by instances. The function also manages the setup based on whether the class is an interface or has a superclass.\n\n**Summary:** This function sets up method information for a class, determining offsets for instance methods in a vtable structure to enable efficient access by instances. It handles static and non-static methods, including those inherited from superclasses, ensuring proper handling of overrides."
