_resolve_class` resolves a class from the constant pool by checking if it's already resolved. If not, it attempts to load the class using its name. If the loaded class meets certain visibility or package conditions, it updates the constant pool and returns the resolved class; otherwise, it sets an exception and returns `NULL`."
